  "instructions": [
    "Season duck thighs with salt and pepper and sear skin side down in 1 tbsp oil until golden and crispy, then flip and cook until internal temperature reaches 165°F (~74°C).",
    "Remove duck, let rest 5 minutes, then dice into bite‑sized pieces and set aside.",
    "In the same pan, add remaining oil, sauté fennel and garlic for 2 minutes until fragrant.",
    "Add ginger and stir quickly for 30 seconds.",
    "Push veggies to side, pour beaten eggs into space, scramble until just set, then mix with veggies.",
    "Add cooked rice, diced duck, soy sauce, oyster sauce, and lime juice; stir fry for 3-4 minutes, ensuring rice grains separate.",
    "Fold in scallions and season with additional salt and pepper to taste.",
    "Serve hot, garnished with extra scallions if desired."
